§ `Part 25 Company charges -- Chapter A1 Registration of company charges -- Company charges (ss 859A to 859G)`

§§ `s 859A Charges created by a company`

-- ---- s 859A(7): the three definitions "In this Part" ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:11611 | “cash” includes foreign currency,
@ref s 859A(7) "cash" (src:11611-11611)
GIVEN `the money is foreign currency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(7) the money is cash` MEANS
    IF `the money is foreign currency`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“cash” includes foreign currency"

-- src:11612 | “charge” includes—
-- src:11613 | (a) a mortgage;
-- src:11614 | (b) a standard security, assignation in security, and any other right in security constituted under the law of Scotland, including any heritable security, but not including a pledge, and
@ref s 859A(7) "charge" (src:11612-11614)
GIVEN `the arrangement is a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement is a standard security, assignation in security, or other right in security constituted under the law of Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement is a pledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(7) the arrangement is a charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the arrangement is a mortgage` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the arrangement is a standard security, assignation in security, or other right in security constituted under the law of Scotland` AND `the arrangement is a pledge`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not including a pledge"
        IF `the arrangement is a standard security, assignation in security, or other right in security constituted under the law of Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“charge” includes—"

-- src:11615 | “company” means a UK-registered company.
@ref s 859A(7) "company" (src:11615-11615)
GIVEN `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(7) the body is a company` MEANS
    IF `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means a UK-registered company"

-- ---- s 859A(6): charges to which the section does not apply -----------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 859A(6) the charge` HAS
    `in favour of a landlord on a cash deposit given as a security in connection with the lease of land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `created by a member of Lloyd's to secure its obligations in connection with its underwriting business at Lloyd's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded from the application of this section by or under any other Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:11606 | (6) This section does not apply to—
-- src:11607 | (a) a charge in favour of a landlord on a cash deposit given as a security in connection with the lease of land;
-- src:11608 | (b) a charge created by a member of Lloyd's (within the meaning of the Lloyd's Act 1982 ) to secure its obligations in connection with its underwriting business at Lloyd's;
-- src:11609 | (c) a charge excluded from the application of this section by or under any other Act.
@ref s 859A(6) This section does not apply to (src:11606-11609)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 859A(6) the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(6) the charge is excluded from the application of section 859A` MEANS
    IF       charge's `in favour of a landlord on a cash deposit given as a security in connection with the lease of land`
         OR  charge's `created by a member of Lloyd's to secure its obligations in connection with its underwriting business at Lloyd's`
         OR  charge's `excluded from the application of this section by or under any other Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text says the section does not apply: "This section does not apply to—"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "This section does not apply to—": the list names three kinds and says nothing of any other charge

-- ---- s 859A(1): when the section applies -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:11601 | (1) Subject to subsection (6), this section applies where a company creates a charge.
@ref s 859A(1) Subject to subsection (6), this section applies where a company creates a charge (src:11601-11601)
GIVEN `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a company creates a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      charge IS A `s 859A(6) the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(1) this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company`) OR (NOT `a company creates a charge`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section applies where a company creates a charge"
        IF (`s 859A(6) the charge is excluded from the application of section 859A` charge) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to—"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 859A(4): the period allowed for delivery -----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:11604 | (4) “The period allowed for delivery” is 21 days beginning with the day after the date of creation of the charge (see section 859E), unless an order allowing an extended period is made under section 859F(3).
@ref s 859A(4) The period allowed for delivery (src:11604-11604)
GIVEN `the date of creation of the charge (section 859E)` IS A DATE
      `the last day to which an order under section 859F(3) extends the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day to which an order under section 859F(3) extends the period`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN lastDay
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the date of creation of the charge (section 859E)`

-- ---- s 859A(2): the registrar's duty to register -----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:11602 | (2) The registrar must register the charge if, before the end of the period allowed for delivery, the company or any person interested in the charge delivers to the registrar for registration a section 859D statement of particulars.
@ref s 859A(2) The registrar must register the charge if (src:11602-11602)
GIVEN `s 859A(1) this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or a person interested in the charge delivers a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 859D(1) what is delivered is a section 859D statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of delivery` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period allowed for delivery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `s 859A(1) this section applies`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section applies where a company creates a charge"
        IF       `the company or a person interested in the charge delivers a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration`
             AND `s 859D(1) what is delivered is a section 859D statement of particulars`
             AND `the day of delivery` AT MOST `the last day of the period allowed for delivery`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must register the charge if, before the end of the period allowed for delivery, the company or any person interested in the charge delivers to the registrar for registration a section 859D statement of particulars"

-- src:11603 | (3) Where the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument, the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars.
@ref s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered (src:11603-11603)
GIVEN `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` MEANS
    IF `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` AND (NOT `a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if": subsection (3) states a necessary condition; the duty itself is in subsection (2)

-- src:11605 | (5) Where an order is made under section 859F(3) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars.
@ref s 859A(5) Where an order is made under section 859F(3) a copy of the order must be delivered (src:11605-11605)
GIVEN `an order is made under section 859F(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(5) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under section 859F(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order is made under section 859F(3)"

-- Subsections (2), (3) and (5) read together (E1 option B: gathered by hand, named for the subsections it gathers). Subsection (5)
-- says only that a copy "must be delivered"; it does not say that the registrar is then not required to register (fork F-A1 in NOTES.md),
-- so an undelivered copy turns a JUST TRUE from (2) into NOTHING, and never into JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 859A(5) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the order is delivered with the statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must register the charge if"
        IF `s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered"
        IF (`s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           AND (`s 859A(5) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           AND (NOT `a copy of the order is delivered with the statement of particulars`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars": subsection (5) does not say what follows if the copy is missing
        IF `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§§ `s 859B Charge in series of debentures`

-- src:11617 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:11618 | (a) a company creates a series of debentures containing a charge, or giving a charge by reference to another instrument, and
-- src:11619 | (b) debenture holders of that series are entitled to the benefit of the charge pari passu.
@ref s 859B(1) This section applies where (src:11617-11619)
GIVEN `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a company creates a series of debentures containing a charge, or giving a charge by reference to another instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `debenture holders of that series are entitled to the benefit of the charge pari passu` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859B(1) this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company`) OR (NOT `a company creates a series of debentures containing a charge, or giving a charge by reference to another instrument`) OR (NOT `debenture holders of that series are entitled to the benefit of the charge pari passu`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where—"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company creates a series of debentures"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instruments are "debentures" is s 738, which another part answers

-- s 859B(6)(a), (b): the period allowed for delivery
-- src:11629 | (6) “The period allowed for delivery” is—
-- src:11630 | (a) if there is a deed containing the charge, 21 days beginning with the day after the date on which the deed is executed;
-- src:11631 | (b) if there is no deed containing the charge, 21 days beginning with the day after the date on which the first debenture of the series is executed.
@ref s 859B(6) The period allowed for delivery (src:11629-11631)
GIVEN `there is a deed containing the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the deed is executed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 859B(6) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` MEANS
    IF `there is a deed containing the charge`
    THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the deed is executed`
    ELSE `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed`

-- s 859B(8): "deed"
-- src:11633 | (8) In this section “ deed ” means—
-- src:11634 | (a) a deed governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland, or
-- src:11635 | (b) an instrument governed by a law other than the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland which requires delivery under that law in order to take effect.
@ref s 859B(8) "deed" (src:11633-11635)
GIVEN `a deed governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an instrument governed by a law other than the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland which requires delivery under that law in order to take effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859B(8) the instrument is a deed` MEANS
    IF `a deed governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` OR `an instrument governed by a law other than the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland which requires delivery under that law in order to take effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “ deed ” means—"

-- s 859B(2): the further particulars
-- src:11620 | (2) The registrar must register the charge if, before the end of the period allowed for delivery, the company or any person interested in the charge delivers to the registrar for registration, a section 859D statement of particulars which also contains the following—
-- src:11621 | (a) either—
-- src:11622 | (i) the name of each of the trustees for the debenture holders, or
-- src:11623 | (ii) where there are more than four such persons, the names of any four persons listed in the charge instrument as trustees for the debenture holders, and a statement that there are other such persons;
-- src:11624 | (b) the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series;
-- src:11625 | (c) the date of the covering instrument (if any) by which the series is created or defined.
@ref s 859B(2) a section 859D statement of particulars which also contains the following (src:11620-11625)
GIVEN `the number of persons who are trustees for the debenture holders` IS A NUMBER
      `the statement gives the name of each of the trustees for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the names of any four persons listed in the charge instrument as trustees for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that there are other such persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a covering instrument by which the series is created or defined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the date of the covering instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` MEANS
    IF       (    `the statement gives the name of each of the trustees for the debenture holders`
              OR  (    `the number of persons who are trustees for the debenture holders` GREATER THAN 4
                   AND `the statement gives the names of any four persons listed in the charge instrument as trustees for the debenture holders`
                   AND `the statement says that there are other such persons`))
         AND `the statement gives the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series`
         AND ((NOT `there is a covering instrument by which the series is created or defined`) OR `the statement gives the date of the covering instrument`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a section 859D statement of particulars which also contains the following—"

-- src:11620 | (2) The registrar must register the charge if, before the end of the period allowed for delivery, the company or any person interested in the charge delivers to the registrar for registration, a section 859D statement of particulars which also contains the following—
@ref s 859B(2) The registrar must register the charge if (src:11620-11620)
GIVEN `s 859B(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company or a person interested in the charge delivers a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 859B(5) the statement is taken to be a section 859D statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day of delivery` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period allowed for delivery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 859B(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where—"
        IF `s 859B(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (1) depends on s 738
        IF       `the company or a person interested in the charge delivers a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration`
             AND `s 859B(5) the statement is taken to be a section 859D statement of particulars`
             AND (`s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             AND `the day of delivery` AT MOST `the last day of the period allowed for delivery`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must register the charge if, before the end of the period allowed for delivery, the company or any person interested in the charge delivers to the registrar for registration, a section 859D statement of particulars which also contains the following—"

-- src:11626 | (3) Where the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument, the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars.
@ref s 859B(3) the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered (src:11626-11626)
GIVEN `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859B(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` MEANS
    IF `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` AND (NOT `a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if": subsection (3) states a necessary condition; the duty itself is in subsection (2)

-- src:11627 | (4) Where the charge is not created or evidenced by an instrument, the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of one of the debentures in the series is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars.
@ref s 859B(4) where the charge is not created or evidenced by an instrument, only if a certified copy of one of the debentures is delivered (src:11627-11627)
GIVEN `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certified copy of one of the debentures in the series is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859B(4) the registrar is required to register the charge` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument`) AND (NOT `a certified copy of one of the debentures in the series is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of one of the debentures in the series is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if": subsection (4) states a necessary condition; the duty itself is in subsection (2)

-- s 859B(5): what is taken to be a section 859D statement. The names of the debenture holders are waived; every other particular
-- of s 859D(1) is still needed (coa19-a1-delivery: `s 859D(1) the statement lacks nothing but possibly the names ...`).
