§§ `s 859C Charges existing on property or undertaking acquired`

-- src:11637 | (1) This section applies where a company acquires property or undertaking which is subject to a charge of a kind which would, if it had been created by the company after the acquisition of the property or undertaking, have been capable of being registered under section 859A.
@ref s 859C(1) This section applies where a company acquires property or undertaking which is subject to a charge (src:11637-11637)
GIVEN `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a company acquires property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or undertaking is subject to a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      charge IS A `s 859A(6) the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859C(1) this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company`) OR (NOT `a company acquires property or undertaking`) OR (NOT `the property or undertaking is subject to a charge`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company acquires property or undertaking which is subject to a charge"
        -- "of a kind which would, if it had been created by the company after the acquisition ..., have been capable of being registered under section 859A":
        -- the same test as s 859A(1), taken as if a company had created the charge.
        IF (`s 859A(1) this section applies` `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` TRUE charge) EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "of a kind which would, if it had been created by the company after the acquisition of the property or undertaking, have been capable of being registered under section 859A"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11638 | (2) The registrar must register the charge if the company or any person interested in the charge delivers to the registrar for registration a section 859D statement of particulars.
@ref s 859C(2) The registrar must register the charge if the company or any person interested in the charge delivers (src:11638-11638)
GIVEN `s 859C(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company or a person interested in the charge delivers a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 859D(1) what is delivered is a section 859D statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 859C(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where"
        IF `the company or a person interested in the charge delivers a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` AND `s 859D(1) what is delivered is a section 859D statement of particulars`
           AND (`s 859C(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 859C(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must register the charge if the company or any person interested in the charge delivers to the registrar for registration a section 859D statement of particulars"

-- src:11639 | (3) Where the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument, the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars.
@ref s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered (src:11639-11639)
GIVEN `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` MEANS
    IF `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` AND (NOT `a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar is required to register it only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if": subsection (3) states a necessary condition; the duty itself is in subsection (2)

GIVEN `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859C(2) and (3) the registrar is required to register the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must register the charge if"
        IF `s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if a certified copy of the instrument is delivered"
        IF `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§§ `s 859D Particulars to be delivered to registrar`

-- What the statement of particulars contains: one BOOLEAN for each particular the section lists, in the section's order.
DECLARE `s 859D what the statement contains` HAS
    `the registered name and number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of creation of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the name of each of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created or of the security agents or trustees holding the charge for the benefit of one or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the names of any four such persons, security agents or trustees listed in the charge instrument, and a statement that there are other such persons, security agents or trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `whether the instrument is expressed to contain a floating charge and, if so, whether it is expressed to cover all the property and undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `whether any of the terms of the charge prohibit or restrict the company from creating further security that will rank equally with or ahead of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `whether (and if so, a short description of) any land, ship, aircraft or intellectual property that is registered or required to be registered in the United Kingdom is subject to a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security included in the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `whether the instrument includes a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security over any tangible or corporeal property, or any intangible or incorporeal property, not described in paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a statement that there is no instrument creating or evidencing the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the names of each of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created or the names of any security agents or trustees holding the charge for the benefit of one or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nature of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a short description of the property or undertaking charged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the obligations secured by the charge` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:11646 | (2) The particulars referred to in subsection (1)(c) are—
-- src:11647 | (a) any of the following—
-- src:11648 | (i) the name of each of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created or of the security agents or trustees holding the charge for the benefit of one or more persons; or,
-- src:11649 | (ii) where there are more than four such persons, security agents or trustees, the names of any four such persons, security agents or trustees listed in the charge instrument, and a statement that there are other such persons, security agents or trustees;
-- src:11650 | (b) whether the instrument is expressed to contain a floating charge and, if so, whether it is expressed to cover all the property and undertaking of the company;
-- src:11651 | (c) whether any of the terms of the charge prohibit or restrict the company from creating further security that will rank equally with or ahead of the charge;
-- src:11652 | (d) whether (and if so, a short description of) any land, ship, aircraft or intellectual property that is registered or required to be registered in the United Kingdom, is subject to a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security included in the instrument;
-- src:11653 | (e) whether the instrument includes a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security over—
-- src:11654 | (i) any tangible or corporeal property, or
-- src:11655 | (ii) any intangible or incorporeal property,
-- src:11656 | not described in paragraph (d).
@ref s 859D(2) The particulars referred to in subsection (1)(c) are (src:11646-11656)
GIVEN contents IS A `s 859D what the statement contains`
      `the number of persons, security agents or trustees in whose favour the charge has been created or who hold it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` MEANS
    IF       (    contents's `the name of each of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created or of the security agents or trustees holding the charge for the benefit of one or more persons`
              OR  (    `the number of persons, security agents or trustees in whose favour the charge has been created or who hold it` GREATER THAN 4
                   AND contents's `the names of any four such persons, security agents or trustees listed in the charge instrument, and a statement that there are other such persons, security agents or trustees`))
         AND contents's `whether the instrument is expressed to contain a floating charge and, if so, whether it is expressed to cover all the property and undertaking of the company`
         AND contents's `whether any of the terms of the charge prohibit or restrict the company from creating further security that will rank equally with or ahead of the charge`
         AND contents's `whether (and if so, a short description of) any land, ship, aircraft or intellectual property that is registered or required to be registered in the United Kingdom is subject to a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security included in the instrument`
         AND contents's `whether the instrument includes a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security over any tangible or corporeal property, or any intangible or incorporeal property, not described in paragraph (d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The particulars referred to in subsection (1)(c) are—"

-- src:11657 | (3) The particulars referred to in subsection (1)(d) are—
-- src:11658 | (a) a statement that there is no instrument creating or evidencing the charge;
-- src:11659 | (b) the names of each of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created or the names of any security agents or trustees holding the charge for the benefit of one or more persons;
-- src:11660 | (c) the nature of the charge;
-- src:11661 | (d) a short description of the property or undertaking charged;
-- src:11662 | (e) the obligations secured by the charge.
@ref s 859D(3) The particulars referred to in subsection (1)(d) are (src:11657-11662)
GIVEN contents IS A `s 859D what the statement contains`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` MEANS
    IF       contents's `a statement that there is no instrument creating or evidencing the charge`
         AND contents's `the names of each of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created or the names of any security agents or trustees holding the charge for the benefit of one or more persons`
         AND contents's `the nature of the charge`
         AND contents's `a short description of the property or undertaking charged`
         AND contents's `the obligations secured by the charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The particulars referred to in subsection (1)(d) are—"

-- s 859D(1): every particular except the names (subsection (2)(a) and (3)(b)), the part that s 859B(5) waives for a series of debentures.
GIVEN contents IS A `s 859D what the statement contains`
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is one to which section 859C applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 859D(1) the statement lacks nothing but possibly the names of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created` MEANS
        contents's `the registered name and number of the company`
    AND contents's `the date of creation of the charge`
    AND ((NOT `the charge is one to which section 859C applies`) OR contents's `the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking concerned`)
    AND (    (`the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument`
              AND contents's `whether the instrument is expressed to contain a floating charge and, if so, whether it is expressed to cover all the property and undertaking of the company`
              AND contents's `whether any of the terms of the charge prohibit or restrict the company from creating further security that will rank equally with or ahead of the charge`
              AND contents's `whether (and if so, a short description of) any land, ship, aircraft or intellectual property that is registered or required to be registered in the United Kingdom is subject to a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security included in the instrument`
              AND contents's `whether the instrument includes a charge (which is not a floating charge) or fixed security over any tangible or corporeal property, or any intangible or incorporeal property, not described in paragraph (d)`)
         OR  ((NOT `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument`)
              AND contents's `a statement that there is no instrument creating or evidencing the charge`
              AND contents's `the nature of the charge`
              AND contents's `a short description of the property or undertaking charged`
              AND contents's `the obligations secured by the charge`))

-- src:11641 | (1) A statement of particulars relating to a charge created by a company is a “section 859D statement of particulars” if it contains the following particulars—
-- src:11642 | (a) the registered name and number of the company;
-- src:11643 | (b) the date of creation of the charge and (if the charge is one to which section 859C applies) the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking concerned;
-- src:11644 | (c) where the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument, the particulars listed in subsection (2);
-- src:11645 | (d) where the charge is not created or evidenced by an instrument, the particulars listed in subsection (3).
@ref s 859D(1) A statement of particulars relating to a charge created by a company is a section 859D statement of particulars if it contains the following particulars (src:11641-11645)
GIVEN contents IS A `s 859D what the statement contains`
      `the number of persons, security agents or trustees in whose favour the charge has been created or who hold it` IS A NUMBER
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is one to which section 859C applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT contents's `the registered name and number of the company`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the registered name and number of the company;"
        IF (NOT contents's `the date of creation of the charge`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the date of creation of the charge"
        IF `the charge is one to which section 859C applies` AND (NOT contents's `the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking concerned`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(if the charge is one to which section 859C applies) the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking concerned"
        IF `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` AND (`s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` contents `the number of persons, security agents or trustees in whose favour the charge has been created or who hold it` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument, the particulars listed in subsection (2)"
        IF (NOT `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument`) AND (`s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` contents EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the charge is not created or evidenced by an instrument, the particulars listed in subsection (3)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 859D(4), (5): the borrowed term and the "includes" definition
-- src:11663 | (4) In this section “ fixed security ” has the meaning given in section 486(1) of the Companies Act 1985 .
@ref s 859D(4) "fixed security" has the meaning given in section 486(1) of the Companies Act 1985 (src:11663-11663)
GIVEN `s 486(1) of the Companies Act 1985 gives the right to the arrangement as fixed security` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859D(4) the arrangement is fixed security` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 486(1) of the Companies Act 1985 gives the right to the arrangement as fixed security`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ fixed security ” has the meaning given in section 486(1) of the Companies Act 1985": the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Companies Act 1985 is not among the sources

-- src:11664 | (5) In this section “ intellectual property ” includes—
-- src:11665 | (a) any patent, trade mark, registered design, copyright or design right;
-- src:11666 | (b) any licence under or in respect of any such right.
@ref s 859D(5) "intellectual property" includes (src:11664-11666)
GIVEN `the right is a patent, trade mark, registered design, copyright or design right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is a licence under or in respect of any such right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859D(5) the right is intellectual property` MEANS
    IF `the right is a patent, trade mark, registered design, copyright or design right` OR `the right is a licence under or in respect of any such right`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“ intellectual property ” includes—"

§§ `s 859E Date of creation of charge`

-- The Table in s 859E(1): one constructor for each row of column 1 (and one for a charge the Table does not describe).
DECLARE `s 859E type of charge` IS ONE OF
    `s 859E a standard security`
    `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and has immediate effect on execution and delivery`
    `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and held in escrow`
    `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and held as undelivered`
    `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by an instrument that is not a deed and has immediate effect on execution`
    `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by an instrument that is not a deed and does not have immediate effect on execution`
    `s 859E a charge not created or evidenced by an instrument`
    `s 859E a charge the Table does not describe`

-- Column 2, row by row. The one DATE input is the date of the event column 2 names for the row:
--   standard security: the date of its recording in the Register of Sasines or its registration in the Land Register of Scotland;
--   deed with immediate effect: the date of delivery; deed held in escrow: the date of delivery into escrow; deed held as undelivered: the date of delivery;
--   instrument that is not a deed, immediate effect: the date of execution; no immediate effect: the date on which the instrument takes effect;
--   no instrument: the date on which the charge comes into effect.
-- src:11668 | (1) For the purposes of this Part, a charge of the type described in column 1 of the Table below is taken to be created on the date given in relation to it in column 2 of that Table.
-- src:11669 | 1. Type of charge | 2. When charge created
-- src:11670 | Standard security | The date of its recording in the Register of Sasines or its registration in the Land Register of Scotland
-- src:11671 | Charge other than a standard security, where created or evidenced by an instrument | Where the instrument is a deed that has been executed and has immediate effect on execution and delivery, the date of delivery
-- src:11672 | Where the instrument is a deed that has been executed and held in escrow, the date of delivery into escrow
-- src:11673 | Where the instrument is a deed that has been executed and held as undelivered, the date of delivery
-- src:11674 | Where the instrument is not a deed and has immediate effect on execution, the date of execution
-- src:11675 | Where the instrument is not a deed and does not have immediate effect on execution, the date on which the instrument takes effect
-- src:11676 | Charge other than a standard security, where not created or evidenced by an instrument | The date on which the charge comes into effect.
@ref s 859E(1) Table: type of charge and when the charge is created (src:11668-11676)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 859E type of charge`
      `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 859E a standard security` THEN JUST `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge`
    WHEN `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and has immediate effect on execution and delivery` THEN JUST `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge`
    WHEN `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and held in escrow` THEN JUST `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge`
    WHEN `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and held as undelivered` THEN JUST `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge`
    WHEN `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by an instrument that is not a deed and has immediate effect on execution` THEN JUST `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge`
    WHEN `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by an instrument that is not a deed and does not have immediate effect on execution` THEN JUST `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge`
    WHEN `s 859E a charge not created or evidenced by an instrument` THEN JUST `the date of the event that column 2 of the Table names for that type of charge`
    WHEN `s 859E a charge the Table does not describe` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Table gives no date for a charge it does not describe

-- src:11677 | (2) Where a charge is created or evidenced by an instrument made between two or more parties, references in the Table in subsection (1) to execution are to execution by all the parties to the instrument whose execution is essential for the instrument to take effect as a charge.
@ref s 859E(2) references in the Table to execution are to execution by all the parties whose execution is essential (src:11677-11677)
GIVEN `every party to the instrument whose execution is essential for it to take effect as a charge has executed it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dates on which those parties executed the instrument` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 859E(2) the date of execution of an instrument made between two or more parties` MEANS
    IF `every party to the instrument whose execution is essential for it to take effect as a charge has executed it` AND (NOT (null `the dates on which those parties executed the instrument`))
    THEN JUST (Date (maximum (map (GIVEN executed YIELD Day executed) `the dates on which those parties executed the instrument`)))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): until every essential party has executed it there is no execution in the Table's sense

-- src:11678 | (3) This section applies for the purposes of this Chapter even if further forms, notices, registrations or other actions or proceedings are necessary to make the charge valid or effectual for any other purposes.
@ref s 859E(3) This section applies for the purposes of this Chapter even if further forms, notices, registrations or other actions or proceedings are necessary (src:11678-11678)
GIVEN `further forms, notices, registrations or other actions or proceedings are necessary to make the charge valid or effectual for any other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859E(3) the date of creation in this section applies for the purposes of Chapter A1` MEANS
    IF `further forms, notices, registrations or other actions or proceedings are necessary to make the charge valid or effectual for any other purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text applies the section "even if" further steps are necessary
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:11679 | (4) For the purposes of this Chapter, the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept a charge as created on the date given as the date of creation of the charge in a section 859D statement of particulars.
@ref s 859E(4) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept a charge as created on the date given (src:11679-11679)
GIVEN `the date is given as the date of creation of the charge in a section 859D statement of particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859E(4) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the charge as created on that date` MEANS
    IF `the date is given as the date of creation of the charge in a section 859D statement of particulars`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the date given as the date of creation of the charge in a section 859D statement of particulars"

-- src:11680 | (5) In this section “ deed ” means—
-- src:11681 | (a) a deed governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland, or
-- src:11682 | (b) an instrument governed by a law other than the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland which requires delivery under that law in order to take effect.
@ref s 859E(5) "deed" (src:11680-11682)
GIVEN `a deed governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an instrument governed by a law other than the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland which requires delivery under that law in order to take effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859E(5) the instrument is a deed` MEANS
    IF `a deed governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` OR `an instrument governed by a law other than the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland which requires delivery under that law in order to take effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “ deed ” means—"

-- src:11683 | (6) References in this section to delivery, in relation to a deed, include delivery as a deed where required.
@ref s 859E(6) References in this section to delivery, in relation to a deed, include delivery as a deed where required (src:11683-11683)
GIVEN `the deed has been delivered as a deed where required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859E(6) a reference to delivery of the deed is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the deed has been delivered as a deed where required`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include delivery as a deed where required"

§§ `s 859F Extension of period allowed for delivery`

-- src:11688 | (2) The requirement is—
-- src:11689 | (a) that the failure to deliver those documents—
-- src:11690 | (i) was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause, or
-- src:11691 | (ii) is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company, or
-- src:11692 | (b) that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief.
@ref s 859F(2) The requirement is (src:11688-11692)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the failure to deliver those documents was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the failure to deliver those documents is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859F(2) the requirement is met` MEANS
    IF       `the court is satisfied that the failure to deliver those documents was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that the failure to deliver those documents is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirement is—"

-- src:11685 | (1) Subsection (3) applies if the court is satisfied that—
-- src:11686 | (a) neither the company nor any other person interested in the charge has delivered to the registrar the documents required under section 859A or (as the case may be) 859B before the end of the period allowed for delivery under the section concerned, and
-- src:11687 | (b) the requirement in subsection (2) is met.
@ref s 859F(1) Subsection (3) applies if the court is satisfied that (src:11685-11687)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that neither the company nor any other person interested in the charge has delivered the documents required under section 859A or 859B before the end of the period allowed for delivery under the section concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 859F(2) the requirement is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859F(1) subsection (3) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the court is satisfied that neither the company nor any other person interested in the charge has delivered the documents required under section 859A or 859B before the end of the period allowed for delivery under the section concerned`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3) applies if the court is satisfied that"
        OTHERWISE `s 859F(2) the requirement is met`

-- src:11693 | (3) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, and on such terms and conditions as seem to the court just and expedient, order that the period allowed for delivery be extended.
@ref s 859F(3) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, order that the period allowed for delivery be extended (src:11693-11693)
GIVEN `s 859F(1) subsection (3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the company or a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859F(3) the court may order that the period allowed for delivery be extended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 859F(1) subsection (3) applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (3) applies if the court is satisfied that": the power is given on that gate and the text does not say it has none otherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the application is made by the company or a person interested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application of the company or a person interested"

§§ `s 859G Personal information etc in certified copies`

DECLARE `s 859G item in a certified copy` IS ONE OF
    `s 859G personal information relating to an individual, other than the name of an individual`
    `s 859G the name of an individual`
    `s 859G the number or other identifier of a bank or securities account of a company or individual`
    `s 859G a signature`
    `s 859G any other item`

-- src:11695 | (1) The following are not required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture delivered to the registrar for the purposes of any provision of this Chapter—
-- src:11696 | (a) personal information relating to an individual (other than the name of an individual);
-- src:11697 | (b) the number or other identifier of a bank or securities account of a company or individual;
-- src:11698 | (c) a signature.
@ref s 859G(1) The following are not required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture (src:11695-11698)
GIVEN item IS A `s 859G item in a certified copy`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859G(1) the item is required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 859G personal information relating to an individual, other than the name of an individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "personal information relating to an individual (other than the name of an individual)"
    WHEN `s 859G the name of an individual` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than the name of an individual)": the carve-out only removes the name from paragraph (a); it does not say the name is required
    WHEN `s 859G the number or other identifier of a bank or securities account of a company or individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the number or other identifier of a bank or securities account of a company or individual"
    WHEN `s 859G a signature` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a signature"
    WHEN `s 859G any other item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) names three kinds of item and says nothing of any other

-- src:11699 | (2) The registrar is entitled without further enquiry, to accept the certified copy of an instrument whether or not any of the information in subsection (1) is contained within the instrument.
@ref s 859G(2) The registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the certified copy of an instrument whether or not any of the information in subsection (1) is contained within the instrument (src:11699-11699)
GIVEN `a certified copy of an instrument is delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the information in subsection (1) is contained within the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859G(2) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the certified copy of the instrument` MEANS
    IF `a certified copy of an instrument is delivered to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether or not any of the information in subsection (1) is contained within the instrument
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the entitlement is to accept a certified copy that has been delivered
